# ---- 23-25: the 2-op FM audition -----------------------------------------
# Am - F - C - G, eight rows a chord, one FM patch per channel: bass on ch0,
# electric piano on ch1, and a bell on ch2 whose rows are eight times as long
# (speed=64, four rows to the other two channels' thirty-two) so that one
# strike rings right through its chord. That bell is also what keeps the
# arrangement off the floor between the eighth-note bass and the comping piano.
# Every FM voice here also carries an ordinary `env`, and ch1 uses the fx
# column - FM is a wave source, so all of that composes exactly as usual.
sfx 23 speed=auto
A2 fm_bass 6
---
A2 fm_bass 4
---
A2 fm_bass 6
